====================================================================
 VENDOR README - THIRD-PARTY CODE IN THIS EXTENSION
====================================================================

This app is fully offline: every runtime asset is vendored in this
directory tree. No CDN, no remote fonts, no network calls at runtime.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
 1. CODEMIRROR 5  >>  codemirror/v5/          (one file per component)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

codemirror v5.65.21: https://codemirror.net/codemirror.zip
  lib,
  mode/*,
  addon/*,
  theme/*,
  keymap/*
  
  all loaded statically by data/interface/index.html script/link tags.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
 2. CODEMIRROR 6  >>  codemirror/v6/          (single reproducible bundle)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Shipped file : codemirror/v6/codemirror.js  (~1.6 MB, minified IIFE)
Exposes      : exactly one global, window.CodeMirror6
Built from   : official npm packages, version-pinned (see section 2.3)

 2.1 WHY A SINGLE BUNDLE (AND NOT ONE FILE PER MODE LIKE V5)?
  CodeMirror 6 does not exist as standalone per-mode / per-addon files.
  The official distribution is a set of ES-modules published on npm
  ("codemirror" + "@codemirror/state", "@codemirror/view",
  "@codemirror/language", "@codemirror/search",
  "@codemirror/autocomplete", "@codemirror/lint",
  "@codemirror/language-data" and the "@lezer/*" parser packages).

These modules import each other by package name, which browsers cannot
resolve without a bundler. Bundling into one IIFE file is the standard,
documented way to vendor CM6 in an extension. All 143 language packages
are embedded inside the bundle (nothing is fetched at runtime).

 2.2 WHERE THE CODE COMES FROM
  - Consumed from : the official npm registry (registry.npmjs.org),
    version-pinned in codemirror/v6/src/package.json and fully locked in
    codemirror/v6/src/package-lock.json.
  - Source code   : https://code.haverbeke.berlin/codemirror (official
    repositories maintained by the CodeMirror author), with read-only
    mirrors on GitHub (github.com/codemirror). The npm tarballs and the
    repositories have identical contents for a given version.

 2.3 DIRECT DEPENDENCIES (exact versions)
  codemirror ................ 6.0.2     (meta package: basicSetup)
  @codemirror/language-data . 6.5.2   (143 languages incl. legacy modes)
  esbuild ................... 0.28.2   (build tool only, never shipped)
  The COMPLETE transitive tree with exact versions is in
  codemirror/v6/src/dependency-tree.txt
  and cryptographically locked in codemirror/v6/src/package-lock.json.

 2.4 HOW TO REBUILD - DETERMINISTIC, BYTE FOR BYTE
  cd codemirror/v6/src
  npm ci               <- installs EXACTLY the locked versions
  node build.mjs       <- bundles + ascii-escapes + writes ../codemirror.js
  The script prints a SHA-256. It must be EXACTLY:

  C359D214835EA300D0BB857DBB4B54F5CBB3E5EE7790A7D7A677C96950C0A281

  If your rebuild hash matches, the shipped file provably contains
  nothing but the pinned public packages plus the small entry source.

 2.5 WHAT GOES INTO THE BUNDLE
  - src/entry.js (~150 lines, human-readable): imports the public CM6
    packages and assigns them to window.CodeMirror6. Nothing else.
  - src/build.mjs (build script): esbuild bundle (IIFE, minified,
    target es2020) followed by an ASCII-normalization pass.
  - ASCII pass: legacy language packs contain raw non-ASCII regex
    literals (e.g. APL glyphs). Raw UTF-8 breaks when a browser decodes
    the file with the wrong charset, so every character >= U+0080 is
    replaced with its \uXXXX escape - semantically byte-identical.
  - Build notes: do NOT use esbuild's --global-name flag; entry.js
    assigns the global itself (a global-name wrapper would clobber it
    with undefined in browsers).

 2.6 RUNTIME SAFETY AUDIT (already performed on the shipped file)
  - zero fetch / XMLHttpRequest / WebSocket / Worker calls
  - zero dynamic import() - every language is embedded in the file
  - the only "http" strings are inert: XML namespaces inside inline
    SVG data-URIs and the "https://" autolink prefix constant
  - no eval / no new Function at import time
  - exactly one global added: window.CodeMirror6

 2.7 FULL-PACKAGE OFFLINE AUDIT (all 449 shipped files scanned)
  - 1163 "http(s)://" string occurrences found; every one of them is
    inert: license headers in vendored files, documentation links in
    comments, or fixture text inside upstream demo/test pages
  - v5 mode folders also contain upstream demo pages (mode/*/index.html)
    and test fixtures (test.js) with sample URLs - these files are NOT
    referenced by index.html or the engine manifest and never load
  - the only script/link injections (resource/config.js engine loader)
    target local extension paths exclusively
  - the service worker (background.js) imports local lib/*.js only
  - binaries: local PNG/GIF icons only
  - conclusion: the package performs zero network activity

--------------------------------------------------------------------
 3. ENGINE SWITCHING
--------------------------------------------------------------------

The active editor version is stored in storage.local "cmv" ("v5" | "v6").
BOTH engines load dynamically through the manifest in resource/config.js
(config.engine.manifest): only the active engine's files are ever loaded.
- v5: 72 CSS + 159 JS files (lib, addons, keymaps, modes, lint backends)
- v6: the single bundle + resource/v6/editor.js + resource/v6/options.js
Engine scripts are injected in manifest order with async=false (ordered
execution), each verified against its expected global where applicable.
The selector is the "API Version" row in the settings sidebar; switching
persists "cmv" and reloads the interface. index.html only carries the
engine-independent core (styles, Sortable, resource/*.js).

